    "show_share": true,
    "description": "The Karachi Electric Supply Company (KESC) and Aga Khan University (AKU) signed an agreement here today for the establishment of a new 132-KV shared grid station. The agreement is a joint venture, where the cost of establishing the station would be shared equally between the two organisations. The new grid station will supply electricity to both the University and KESC's consumers in the area. KESC CEO, Tabish Gauhar and Aga Khan University President, Firoz Rasul signed the agreement.",
